---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Navbar from "../components/Navbar.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";
---

<Layout 
  title="Terms & Conditions — LIFT Due Diligence Operating System" 
  description="Master institutional terms of service governing participation across GGAM Advisory, incubator cohorts, and venture data rooms."
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="flex-1 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      
      <!-- Header -->
      <div class="mb-12 border-b border-white/10 pb-8">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-indigo-500/10 border border-indigo-500/20 text-indigo-400 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">
          Master Legal Framework
        </div>
        <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-white font-heading tracking-tight">
          Terms & Conditions of Service
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-4 text-slate-400 text-sm sm:text-base">
          Last Updated: September 2026 · GGAM Advisory & LIFT Ecosystem
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Content Sections -->
      <div class="space-y-10 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">
        
        <section class="glass-panel rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-white/5 space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-heading flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple-400"></span>
            1. Acceptance of Master Terms
          </h2>
          <p>
            By accessing or authenticating into any portal within the LIFT ecosystem—including <code class="text-purple-300 font-mono text-xs">admin.lift.business</code>, <code class="text-blue-300 font-mono text-xs">portal.lift.business</code>, or <code class="text-emerald-300 font-mono text-xs">app.lift.business</code>—you agree to be bound by these Master Terms and Conditions. If you represent an institutional entity, incubator, or startup enterprise, you attest that you possess authorized signatory authority.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="glass-panel rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-white/5 space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-heading flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple-400"></span>
            2. Platform Roles & Authorized Permitted Use
          </h2>
          <p>
            LIFT operates as a diligence orchestration infrastructure. Platform use is categorized by distinct access domains:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-slate-300">
            <li><strong class="text-white">Advisory Terminal (GGAM):</strong> Authorized solely for formal due diligence evaluation, scoring index compilation, and investment committee memo preparation.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Incubator Cohort Hub:</strong> Authorized for accelerator directors, government grant officers, and program managers monitoring founder compliance milestones.</li>
            <li><strong class="text-white">Startup Data Room:</strong> Authorized for venture founders and designated CFOs to submit statutory documentation, reconcile queries, and certify cap table integrity.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="glass-panel rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-white/5 space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-heading flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple-400"></span>
            3. Warranty of Accuracy & Document Integrity
          </h2>
          <p>
            Parties uploading financial filings, MCA registry returns, capitalization tables, or IP documentation warrant that all submitted records are authentic, unaltered, and reflect true statutory filings. Intentional submission of falsified balance sheets, forged board resolutions, or misrepresented cap tables constitutes immediate termination of access and statutory legal referral.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="glass-panel rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-white/5 space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-heading flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple-400"></span>
            4. Mutual Non-Disclosure & Fiduciary Confidentiality
          </h2>
          <p>
            All non-public proprietary materials deposited in a venture data room shall be treated as strictly Confidential Information. Users shall not capture, bypass watermarking, replicate, reverse-engineer, or transmit confidential files to unauthorized third parties outside the agreed investment syndicate scope.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="glass-panel rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-white/5 space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-heading flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple-400"></span>
            5. Intellectual Property Rights & Data Ownership
          </h2>
          <p>
            The startup enterprise retains full and exclusive ownership of all uploaded corporate assets, trade secrets, software escrow repositories, and proprietary pitch documentation. LIFT and GGAM Advisory acquire no ownership, title, or patent rights by virtue of hosting or indexing materials for diligence analysis.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="glass-panel rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-white/5 space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-heading flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple-400"></span>
            6. Limitation of Liability & Diligence Disclaimers
          </h2>
          <p>
            While LIFT utilizes sophisticated automated verification engines, OCR algorithms, and cross-registry validations, the calculated Diligence Index and automated AI flags are decision-support frameworks. Final capital allocation, syndication, and investment decisions remain the sole responsibility of participating Investment Committees and accredited syndicates.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section class="glass-panel rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 border border-white/5 space-y-4">
          <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-white font-heading flex items-center gap-3">
            <span class="w-2 h-2 rounded-full bg-purple-400"></span>
            7. Governing Jurisdiction & Dispute Resolution
          </h2>
          <p>
            These terms are governed by and construed under institutional commercial arbitration guidelines. Any disputes arising in connection with platform operations shall be referred to institutional arbitration in accordance with applicable rules.
          </p>
        </section>

      </div>

      <!-- Return Link -->
      <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-white/10 text-center">
        <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-purple-400 hover:text-purple-300 font-medium transition-colors">
          &larr; Back to LIFT Home
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
